# Phase 2: Build MVP Core

## Overview

Build the core infrastructure: URL scraper, channel database, simple UI, and payment. NO AI matching yet — that's Phase 3. This phase delivers a manually-curated version that proves the value prop.

## Requirements

- Functional: User pastes URL → sees product analysis + channel recommendations
- Non-functional: <3s response time, mobile-friendly, works on Cloudflare free tier

## Architecture

```
User → Landing Page (HTMX)
  → Paste URL form
  → POST /api/analyze
    → Scrape URL (Cheerio)
    → Extract: title, description, features, pricing, category
    → Match against channel DB (keyword matching v1)
    → Return ranked channels + generic outreach templates
  → Results page (server-rendered)
  → Stripe checkout ($19/mo or $9 one-time)
```

## Related Code Files

- Create: `src/index.ts` — Hono worker entry point
- Create: `src/scraper.ts` — URL scraper (Cheerio + fetch)
- Create: `src/channels.ts` — Channel database + matching
- Create: `src/templates/` — HTML templates (landing, results, payment)
- Create: `src/data/channels.json` — Initial channel database
- Create: `wrangler.toml` — Cloudflare Workers config
- Create: `package.json`

## Implementation Steps

### Step 1: Project Setup (2h)

1. Init project:
   ```bash
   mkdir distro-intel && cd distro-intel
   npm init -y
   npm install hono @hono/node-server cheerio stripe
   npm install -D wrangler typescript @types/node
   ```

2. Configure `wrangler.toml`:
   ```toml
   name = "distro-intel"
   main = "src/index.ts"
   compatibility_date = "2026-05-01"
   [vars]
   ENVIRONMENT = "production"
   ```

3. Create Hono entry point with routes:
   - `GET /` → landing page
   - `POST /api/analyze` → analysis endpoint
   - `GET /results/:id` → results page
   - `POST /api/checkout` → Stripe redirect

### Step 2: URL Scraper (4h)

4. Build scraper module:
   - Fetch URL with timeout (5s)
   - Extract with Cheerio: `<title>`, `<meta name="description">`, `<h1>`, `<h2>`, pricing text
   - Detect category: SaaS, marketplace, mobile app, Chrome extension, API, template, content
   - Extract features from bullet points / feature lists
   - Handle errors gracefully (404, timeout, blocked)
   - Output: `ProductProfile` object

   ```typescript
   interface ProductProfile {
     url: string;
     title: string;
     description: string;
     category: 'saas' | 'marketplace' | 'api' | 'extension' | 'template' | 'content' | 'other';
     features: string[];
     pricing: string | null;
     targetAudience: string | null;
   }
   ```

### Step 3: Channel Database (4h)

5. Build initial channel database (500 entries):
   - 200 Reddit subreddits (categorized by: dev, design, startup, niche-specific)
   - 100 Discord servers (builder communities)
   - 100 Facebook groups (global + VN)
   - 50 forums (HN, IndieHackers, ProductHunt, niche forums)
   - 50 other (Twitter hashtags, newsletters accepting submissions, podcasts)

6. Each channel entry:
   ```json
   {
     "id": "reddit-sideproject",
     "platform": "reddit",
     "name": "r/SideProject",
     "url": "https://reddit.com/r/SideProject",
     "category": ["saas", "marketplace", "api", "template"],
     "audience_size": 150000,
     "commercial_tolerance": "high",
     "best_format": "Show post with value-first framing",
     "best_timing": "Tuesday-Thursday, 9-11 AM EST",
     "dont_do": "Don't post direct pitch, provide value first",
     "tags": ["launch", "feedback", "side-project"]
   }
   ```

7. Keyword-based matching v1 (no AI yet):
   - Match product category → channel categories
   - Rank by: relevance score × audience_size × commercial_tolerance
   - Return top 15 channels

### Step 4: UI (3h)

8. Landing page — use exact language from Phase 1 discovery:
   - Hero: "Built something great? Find your first 50 users."
   - Subhead: "Paste your URL. Get a ranked list of WHERE to post + WHAT to say."
   - Single input: URL field + "Analyze" button
   - Social proof section (add after first users)

9. Results page:
   - Product summary card (what we detected)
   - Ranked channel list (15 channels)
   - Each channel: name, why relevant, audience size, best format, timing, template
   - CTA: "Get full report with AI-powered scripts" → Stripe

10. Keep styling minimal: system fonts, 1 accent color, no framework

### Step 5: Payment Integration (2h)

11. Stripe setup:
    - Product: "Distribution Intelligence Report"
    - Price 1: $9 one-time (single report)
    - Price 2: $19/mo (unlimited reports)
    - Checkout flow: results preview (5 channels free) → full report (15 channels + scripts) behind paywall
    - Webhook: `POST /api/webhook` → mark user as paid

## Success Criteria

- [ ] `wrangler dev` runs locally without errors
- [ ] URL scraper extracts product info from 10 test URLs correctly
- [ ] Channel database has 500+ entries with categories
- [ ] Matching returns relevant channels (manual QA: 8/10 relevance)
- [ ] Landing page renders on mobile
- [ ] Stripe checkout flow works end-to-end
- [ ] Deployed to Cloudflare Workers (`wrangler deploy`)
- [ ] Total infra cost <$10/mo

## Risk Assessment

| Risk | Probability | Mitigation |
|------|-------------|------------|
| Scraping blocked by target sites | 20% | Use OG meta tags as fallback; most indie sites don't block |
| Channel DB too generic | 30% | Start with 200 high-quality entries, expand based on user feedback |
| Cloudflare Worker limits hit | 10% | Free tier = 100K req/day; won't hit this at MVP stage |
| Stripe setup complexity | 5% | Standard integration, well-documented |
